course: dictionary
lesson: 2002
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them shows which one you need. The word is «concern». Read the words next to it, then ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «The IUCN Red List records how endangered each species is, from least concern through vulnerable, endangered and critically endangered to extinct.» Here «least concern» is a level on a list, the lowest level of danger for a species. Concern is not a feeling in this sentence.
explain: Now read «This letter concerns your child's trip.» Concerns is a verb here, and it means is about. A quick check works: swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. «This letter is about your child's trip» does.
fact: A concern (noun) is a worry about something, as in «If you have any concerns, tell a teacher.»
fact: Concern (verb) can mean to worry someone, or to be about something or to involve someone.
fact: «Concerned about» means worried about something, as in «I am concerned about the rain.»
fact: Something that is your business or responsibility can be a concern, as in «It's no concern of yours.»
fact: In formal writing, a concern can also mean a business or company.
exercise: «The IUCN Red List records how endangered each species is, from least concern through vulnerable, endangered and critically endangered to extinct.» In this sentence, what does least concern describe? | A kind of animal | *The lowest level of danger for a species | The most worrying level of danger | A list of school trips
exercise: «This letter concerns your child's trip.» What does concerns mean here? | Stops the trip | Pays for the trip | *Is about the trip | Worries the trip
exercise: Mum says, «I'm concerned about the rain.» What does concerned mean? | Happy | Asleep | Bored | *Worried
test: «If you have any concerns, tell a teacher.» What is a concern in this sentence? | A school trip | A prize | *A worry | A kind of teacher
test: «It's no concern of yours.» What does this mean? | It is your favourite game | It is very loud | *It is not your business | It is a big worry for you
exam: Which meaning fits «The meeting concerns the new playground»? | It is a prize for the playground | It is a worry about the playground | It is a long walk to the playground | *It is about the new playground
